# brixels.pdl - SEED vocabulary for brixels (2026-10-12, claude). The owner's words (handoff doc section 0): "in-house art ... evolving shape-clay used as Lego-like pieces ... an image concept bank (images associated by pixel maps) says what a piece looks like and what it does ... pieces socket together: arms + legs + head = a human; wheels + engine + windshield = a car."
# Everything below is a PROPOSAL for Grok to confirm or replace (see design-docs/BRIXELS-DESIGN.md). Nothing reads this file yet. Sizes are in voxels on the same 16-grid as the engine's emoji voxel models (voxels_16.csv).
# BRIXEL | id | kind | w | h | d | note                 one drawable piece (w x h x d voxels; x = left-right, y = front-back, z = up)
# SOCKET | brixel | name | type | x | y | z | facing     where another piece plugs in; type must match the plugging piece's PLUG row; facing = n e s w up down
# PLUG   | brixel | name | type | x | y | z | facing     the piece's own connector
# ASSEMBLY | id | role | brixel | on_socket | note        a recipe: ROLE says what the assembled thing is (car, person); on_socket = the parent socket it plugs into (root = the first row)
# CONCEPT | brixel | image | pixelmap | does              the concept bank row: an image (path, may be a CDDA/emoji id) associated with the piece by a pixel map file, and a sentence for what the piece DOES (an events-hq / blueprintz hook, not code)
BRIXEL | car_frame | body | 8 | 4 | 2 | the chassis; every other car piece plugs into it
BRIXEL | car_wheel | wheel | 2 | 2 | 2 | rolls; one per corner
BRIXEL | car_engine | engine | 3 | 3 | 2 | gives speed; sits in the engine bay
BRIXEL | car_windshield | glass | 4 | 1 | 2 | front glass
BRIXEL | car_door | door | 2 | 1 | 2 | opens (events: door_open / door_closed)
BRIXEL | car_seat | seat | 2 | 2 | 2 | where a person sits
BRIXEL | car_roof | roof | 4 | 4 | 1 | hides the interior from above (roofs hide when the camera is inside, same rule as buildings)
BRIXEL | car_headlight | light | 1 | 1 | 1 | light
BRIXEL | person_torso | body | 3 | 2 | 4 | the root of a person
BRIXEL | person_head | head | 2 | 2 | 2 | 
BRIXEL | person_arm | limb | 1 | 1 | 4 | one per side
BRIXEL | person_leg | limb | 1 | 1 | 4 | one per side
